==Latin==

===Etymology===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*(s)kewH-}}
From {{inh|la|itc-pro|*kutis}}, from {{der|la|ine-pro||*kuH-t-}}, {{glossary|zero-grade}} form of {{m|ine-pro|*(s)kewH-||to cover}} without {{glossary|s-mobile}}.

Cognates include {{cog|grc|σκύλος||hide}}, {{cog|cy|cwd||scrotum}}, {{cog|lt|kutỹs||purse}}, {{cog|ang|hȳd}} ({{cog|en|hide}}), {{m+|ang|scēo||sky}} ({{m+|en|sky}}), {{cog|de|Haut||skin}}, {{cog|de|Hoden||scrotum}} and {{cog|sa|स्कुनाति|tr=skunā́ti|t=to cover}}. Related to {{m|la|culus}}.

